<LessonFrame Number="8">
    <Try>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Open <b>Reactor</b>. It counts, and the core pulses.</li>
            <li>Type a note in <b>Hangar</b>, then open <b>Observatory</b> and type a note there too.</li>
            <li>Go back to the Reactor. The count carried on from where it was, and it says it was <i>paused</i> while you were away.</li>
            <li>Go back to Hangar: your note is still there. Go back to the Observatory: its note is gone, because that page is not kept alive.</li>
            <li>Notice the fade as the pages change. That is a view transition, turned on once in <code>Program.cs</code>.</li>
        </ol>
    </Try>
    <Stage>
        <XRay Name="Lesson8Page" Level="0">
            <nav class="tabs" aria-label="Pages">
                <RouteLink Route="reactor" Class="tab">Reactor</RouteLink>
                <RouteLink Route="hangar" Class="tab">Hangar</RouteLink>
                <RouteLink Route="observatory" Class="tab">Observatory</RouteLink>
            </nav>
            <div class="tab-body">
                <ModRouterOutlet>
                    <EmptyContent><p class="dim">Pick a page.</p></EmptyContent>
                </ModRouterOutlet>
            </div>
        </XRay>
    </Stage>
    <Code>
        <CodeRef File="LabRoutes.cs"><code>.KeepAlive(3)</code> on two routes, and none on the third</CodeRef>
        <CodeRef File="Lessons/L8/ReactorPage.razor.cs"><code>IKeepAliveRoute</code>: pause when hidden, resume when shown</CodeRef>
        <CodeRef File="Program.cs"><code>options.ViewTransitions.Enabled</code></CodeRef>
    </Code>
</LessonFrame>
